<title>USA: N.Y. BUSINESS LOANS FELL $557 MLN IN JULY 30 WEEK.</title>
<headline>N.Y. BUSINESS LOANS FELL $557 MLN IN JULY 30 WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $557 million to $46,676 million in the week ended July 30, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $557 million to $46,955 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $3,992 million to $875,839 million.</p>
<p>(( -- Caryn Trokie, 212-859-1678 ))</p>
